# Synthesis cache -- deliberately NOT committed.
#
# 375 files, 72 MB, and it grows with every measurement. More importantly it is
# keyed on the SDK version: cache_key() in oracle/measure.py hashes
# classiq.__version__ and COMPILER_VERSION alongside the design, so every entry
# here belongs to classiq 1.28.0 and becomes unreachable the moment you install
# 1.29.0. It is a speed optimisation, not a record.
#
# The record is logs/experiments.jsonl, which IS committed: 595 rows, width,
# depth, cx and settings for every design ever measured. That file cost about
# 6.6 hours of cloud time and cannot be regenerated cheaply.
#
# To carry the cache to another machine anyway (it tars down to 4 MB):
#     tar -czf cache.tgz cache/
# and restore with  tar -xzf cache.tgz  next to the repo. Only worth doing if
# you pin classiq==1.28.0, which requirements.txt does.
cache/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Credentials -- classiq stores an auth token after `classiq.authenticate()`.
.env
*.token

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# c++ packages
cpp/vendor/
cpp/build/

.vscode/